    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d4">

                <pb facs="0052" n="806" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v02/pg806"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/3505</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Netherlands</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Langhorne</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">The Hague</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-04-18T11:00:00+01:19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 18, 1917, 11 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 4.15 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>863. Have been informally and confidentially approached by member of British
                    Legation here regarding attitude which Government of the United States intends
                    to adopt towards American citizens of enemy origin whose business transactions
                    may be under suspicion, and regarding possibility that United States will adopt
                    system of black list similar to British. Respectfully ask instructions in
                    premises.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Langhorne</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
